# Job control's calls (roadmap os-server.md P11): with no program the root
# builds (program: none), init starts tests/posix/jobs.c (TEST_POSIX_JOBS):
# a session whose terminal it is, groups and their refusals, kill to a
# group, SIGSTOP and SIGCONT as waitpid (WUNTRACED, WCONTINUED) and SIGCHLD
# see them, SA_NOCLDSTOP, a stop in a pipe's read, ^Z for the foreground's
# reader, SIGTTIN and EIO for a background reader, SIGTTOU for a
# background writer with TOSTOP and for tcsetpgrp.
program: none
define: TEST_POSIX_JOBS
keys: {ctrl-z}
match: contains
---
jobs: setsid (my pid): 1
jobs: setsid again (-1, EPERM 1): -1, 1
jobs: getsid(0), getpgrp (mine): 1 1
jobs: tcgetpgrp before the terminal is ours (-1, ENOTTY 1): -1, 1
jobs: tcgetpgrp once opened (mine 1): 1
jobs: setpgid to no group (-1, EPERM 1): -1, 1
jobs: kill a group of two (0): 0
jobs: its first: signal 15
jobs: its second: signal 15
jobs: SIGSTOP, WUNTRACED: stopped 19; SIGCHLD 1
jobs: SIGCONT, WCONTINUED: continued
jobs: its handler ran, then it ended: exit 7
jobs: SA_NOCLDSTOP: stopped 19; SIGCHLD 0
jobs: stopped in a read, continued, it read on: exit 8
^Z
jobs: ^Z: stopped 20
jobs: a background read: stopped 21
jobs: ... SIGTTIN ignored, EIO: exit 9
jobs: a background write without TOSTOP
jobs: ... it went: exit 10
jobs: a background write with TOSTOP: stopped 22
jobs: tcsetpgrp from the background: stopped 22
jobs: done
